  <h2 id="filter-menu-search">Filter Menu With Search</h2>
  <p>
    A <code>filter-menu__header</code> holds a search field for a long list of
    choices. Skin styles the field; hiding the choices that do not match is up
    to script, which this example does not include. The field needs an
    accessible name, and <code>aria-controls</code> points it at the menu it
    narrows.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="demo__inner">
      <span class="filter-menu">
        <div class="filter-menu__header">
          <svg class="icon icon--16" height="16" width="16" aria-hidden="true">
            <icon-symbol name="search-16"/>
          </svg>
          <input
            type="text"
            class="filter-menu__search"
            placeholder="Search"
            aria-label="Search brands"
            aria-controls="filter-menu-search-items"
          >
          <button
            type="button"
            class="icon-button icon-button--transparent"
            aria-label="Clear search"
          >
            <svg
              class="icon icon--20"
              height="20"
              width="20"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <icon-symbol name="clear-20"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div
          class="filter-menu__items"
          role="menu"
          aria-label="Brand"
          id="filter-menu-search-items"
        >
          <div
            class="filter-menu__item"
            role="menuitemcheckbox"
            aria-checked="false"
            tabindex="0"
